  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support adequate housing efforts in Latin America</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Latin America, between 50 and 75% of living spaces are the result of a non-market production, developed by the inhabitants, with socio,cultural, environmental and economical benefits that conceives housing as a process that even creates bonds with the territory and community: the Social Production of Habitat (SPH). This project will support a Regional Working Group (RWG) of organizations and movements that seeks to broaden the recognition of SPH and realice the right to adequate housing.</narrative>
  </description>
